  "designRules": [
    "Opening deployments are movable state, not permanent combat bonuses.",
    "Long deployments accumulate fatigue and sustainment strain; fresh surge deployments begin at higher readiness.",
    "Russia and Ukraine begin with almost all mobile conventional manoeuvre power committed to the line of contact.",
    "European coalition power is distributed across sovereign members; Greenland response forces and the eastern land front compete for readiness, shipping, airlift and stocks.",
    "China begins with a substantial but not total share of deployable power committed to maintaining the Taiwan blockade and holding an escalation reserve.",
    "Taiwan begins on full alert with most deployable forces assigned to island and maritime defence.",
    "Rear areas retain strategic air defence, base and nuclear security, training and reconstitution functions rather than being literally undefended.",
    "Redeploying forces away from an active theatre weakens that theatre immediately and requires travel and logistics time."
  ]
